              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: multipartFile.getOriginalFilename(). Sink: Path resolution at line 75 (destinationDir.toPath().resolve(...)). Dataflow: The user-supplied filename is used directly in `resolve()` without sanitization. An attacker can supply a filename like '../../evil.sh' to traverse outside the intended directory. No sanitization is performed on the filename before reaching the file system sink. Conclusion: This is a path traversal vulnerability."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: multipartFile.getOriginalFilename(). Sink: Path resolution at line 75 (destinationDir.toPath().resolve(...)). Dataflow: The user-supplied filename is used directly in `resolve()` without sanitization. An attacker can supply a filename like '../../evil.sh' to traverse outside the intended directory. No sanitization is performed on the filename before reaching the file system sink. Conclusion: This is a path traversal vulnerability."
          },
