          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The 'column' parameter from @RequestParam. Sink: connection.prepareStatement on line 53 involving concatenation. Dataflow: The user-supplied 'column' string is concatenated directly into the SQL query string used to create a PreparedStatement. Sanitization: There is no validation or allow-listing of the 'column' input before it is embedded into the query. Since SQL identifiers like column names cannot be parameterized, this allows for SQL injection. Conclusion: Confirmed SQL injection vulnerability."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-sqli",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: The 'column' parameter from @RequestParam. Sink: connection.prepareStatement on line 53 involving concatenation. Dataflow: The user-supplied 'column' string is concatenated directly into the SQL query string used to create a PreparedStatement. Sanitization: There is no validation or allow-listing of the 'column' input before it is embedded into the query. Since SQL identifiers like column names cannot be parameterized, this allows for SQL injection. Conclusion: Confirmed SQL injection vulnerability."
          },
