              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The templateName variable, derived from the template/resourceName parameter which originates from Thymeleaf templates (e.g., \u003cdiv th:replace='~{doc:filename.adoc}'\u003e\u003c/div\u003e).\n\nSink: line 95, where resourceLoader.getResource('classpath:/' + templateName).getInputStream() is called.\n\nDataflow: The templateName taken from the Thymeleaf tag is passed to getInputStream, which uses it to build a Spring resource path without validation.\n\nSanitization: None.\n\nConclusion: The code suffers from a path traversal vulnerability as it allows arbitrary files to be loaded from the classpath."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: The templateName variable, derived from the template/resourceName parameter which originates from Thymeleaf templates (e.g., \u003cdiv th:replace='~{doc:filename.adoc}'\u003e\u003c/div\u003e).\n\nSink: line 95, where resourceLoader.getResource('classpath:/' + templateName).getInputStream() is called.\n\nDataflow: The templateName taken from the Thymeleaf tag is passed to getInputStream, which uses it to build a Spring resource path without validation.\n\nSanitization: None.\n\nConclusion: The code suffers from a path traversal vulnerability as it allows arbitrary files to be loaded from the classpath."
          },
